        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071103/assets/190af2ef92a8c23efb6fc15c6effebf5db929d8d133da6809bd27f77a6e9292b.png)\n\nThe vector $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $-1.$ Find the vector $Av.$",
        "worked_solution": "The eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =-1v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071103/assets/1f778e38d2dd4d2e33675bfa45bbe13c9596b1818092ef6129e8f35b1741157e.png)",
